{"name":"Woven Basket","hex":"#8e7b58","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fabricated by weaving.","Interlaced"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cloth formed by weaving. It only stretches in the bias directions (between the warp and weft directions), unless the threads are elastic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woven"},{"term":"basket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight woven container, generally round, open at the top, and tapering toward the bottom.","A bed for a cat."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a basket or baskets.","To cross-collateralize the royalty advances for multiple works so that the creator is not paid until all of those works have achieved a certain level of success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woven fabric","blocks":[{"text":"Woven fabric is any textile formed by weaving. Woven fabrics, often created on a loom, are made of many threads woven in a warp and weft. Technically, a woven fabric is any fabric made by interlacing two or more threads at right angles to one another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg/330px-Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woven_fabric","wikidata":"Q1314278"},{"title":"Basket","blocks":[{"text":"A basket is a container that is traditionally constructed from stiff fibers, and can be made from a range of materials, including wood splints, runners, and cane. While most baskets are made from plant materials, other materials such as horsehair, baleen, or metal wire can be used. Baskets are generally woven by hand. Some baskets are fitted with a lid, while others are left open on top."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Baskets_in_Haikou_03.jpg/330px-Baskets_in_Haikou_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basket","wikidata":"Q201097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG/500px-Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG/500px-Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Arabic-language graphic distinguishing raw fibers from processed threads and woven fabric.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFabric_yarn_fiber.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Leinengewebe.JPG/500px-Leinengewebe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Leinengewebe.JPG/1280px-Leinengewebe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Leinengewebe.JPG/500px-Leinengewebe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plain weave","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeinengewebe.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg/500px-Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg/1280px-Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg/500px-Audiniu_pavyzdziai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Types of woven textiles for dresses.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki